# Movago — Cursor rules

Follow `docs/STRUCTURE.md` as the source of truth for folder layout, brand, and product scope. Do not invent new top-level folders without updating that doc.

## Role

Act as a senior website developer for MOVAGO. When analyzing or fixing issues:

- Diagnose precisely — identify the root cause, not just the symptom
- Prefer the strongest solution for a **premium** experience over quick hacks
- Explain trade-offs briefly when recommending an approach
- Optimize for user trust: the product should feel calm, polished, and **safe** (clear UX, reliable flows, careful handling of booking/auth/location data)

Ship work that matches executive-transfer quality: refined UI, solid correctness, and confidence for the customer.

## Product

MOVAGO — premium **chauffeur-driven** car rental / executive airport transfer.

Core capabilities the product must support:

- Book and manage trips on the website (`/book` and booking flows)
- Member accounts (register, login, profile, booking history)
- Location pick-up / drop-off via **Google Maps place search** or **custom map pin**
- Marketing pages: Home, Services, Vehicles, Destinations, Corporate, About

## Brand theme (from design)

Dark luxury + gold accent. Do not invent alternate palettes (no purple gradients, no emerald primary).

| Token | Value | Usage |
|-------|-------|--------|
| Background | `#000000` | page / hero dark surfaces |
| Surface | `#141414` / `#1A1A1A` | cards, panels, footer blocks |
| Accent gold | `#C5A073` | CTA buttons, active nav, icons, highlights |
| Accent gold hover | `#B08D60` | button / link hover |
| Text primary | `#FFFFFF` | headings, primary copy on dark |
| Text secondary | `#B3B3B3` | body / muted on dark |
| Text on gold | `#000000` | label on gold buttons |
| Light section bg | `#F3F3F3` | occasional light bands (amenities bars) |

Typography:

- Headings: **Playfair Display** (serif, luxury)
- Body / nav / forms: **Inter** (sans-serif)
- **Default text size = 16px** (`text-base`) for body, table, buttons, inputs, labels, errors
- Avoid `text-sm` / `text-xs` except badges, captions, metadata
- Section titles use `text-lg` and up — never shrink body below 16px
- Content canvas: `.page-width` = `width: 1440px; margin: auto;` (`max-width: 100%` on smaller viewports)

## Structure (summary)

- Routes only in `app/` (marketing group + `book` + future auth/member routes)
- `components/layout` — Header, Footer, Navbar
- `ui/` — shared primitives (Button, Input, Select, Icon, …)
- `components/<feature>` — home, vehicles, destinations, corporate, about, services, booking, membership, maps
- `constants`, `data`, `hooks`, `lib`, `services`, `styles`, `types`, `utils`
- Maps / Places API clients → `lib/`; booking & membership domain → `services/`
- Assets in `public/images/*` and `public/icons`
- Experiments only in `_sandbox/`

## Do

- Keep `page.tsx` thin; compose from `components/`
- Put API/domain logic in `lib/` or `services/`
- Use `@/` imports
- Match naming: PascalCase components, camelCase utils
- Use brand gold for primary CTAs (`Book Now`, Search, submit) via `constants/theme` + `utils/ui/button` — do not hardcode button colors in UI
- Location UX must support both Places autocomplete and manual pin drop

## Do not

- Put business logic or shared components under `app/`
- Scatter fetch calls inside UI components
- Add production features under `_sandbox/`
- Create alternate trees like `src/components` or random root folders
- Override default body text to smaller than `text-base`
- Use non-brand primary colors (emerald, purple, etc.)
